.\" Leon Build Tool — Man Page
.TH LBT 1 "2026-08-07" "lbt 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbt \- Leon Build Tool: run the boot-manager TUI, manage boot config, inspect geometry and boot entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbt
.B info
.RI [ dump ]
.br
.B lbt
.B discover
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B lbt
.B tui
.br
.B lbt
.B config
.B get
.RI [ key ]
.B | set
.I key
.I value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbt
is the host-side companion to the Leon bootloader. It introspects the live
machine (block devices, EFI System Partitions, boot entries, framebuffer and
BGRT logo geometry), launches a full-screen keyboard-driven boot-manager menu
(a pure-Rust ratatui app, no embedded Python), and edits the boot
configuration consumed by the bootloader.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS info
Print the current framebuffer and BGRT logo geometry.
.TP
.B info \fIdump\
With a path to a geometry record (\fIbootinfo.json\fR written by the
bootloader to \eEFI\eleon), print the captured geometry instead of the live one.
.TP
.B info
Without an argument, read live geometry from /sys
(/sys/class/graphics/fb0 and /sys/firmware/acpi/bgrt). Fails loudly if no live
framebuffer is available rather than guessing.
.SS discover
Auto-detect every EFI System Partition and its boot entries.
Note: In addition to enumerating mounted ESPs, Leon scans common `/boot`
locations (`/boot`, `/boot/efi`, `/boot/EFI`) recursively for EFI-capable
files and includes them as candidate boot entries. Detection is strict: `.efi`
files must validate as PE/COFF (`MZ` + `PE\0\0`) and ELF files must contain the
`EFI stub` marker in the first 64 KiB to be accepted as an EFI-stub kernel.
.TP
.B discover
List block devices (name, kind, filesystem, mount point), ESPs, and boot entries.
.TP
.B discover \-\-json
Emit the same information as machine-readable JSON with the keys
.BR devices ,
.BR esps ,
and
.BR boot_entries .
.SS tui
Launch the Leon boot-manager menu: a full-screen, keyboard-driven ratatui app
that mirrors what the bootloader renders at boot. Before it runs, lbt exports
the live framebuffer + BGRT geometry, the discovered boot entries, and the boot
config as
.I LEON_*
environment variables
(\fILEON_FB_WIDTH\fR, \fILEON_FB_HEIGHT\fR, \fILEON_FB_STRIDE\fR,
\fILEON_FB_FORMAT\fR, \fILEON_BOOT_ENTRIES\fR with one
\fIlabel<TAB>path\fR per line). Entries normally come from live discovery
(.efi PE/COFF binaries and EFI-stub ELF kernels on mounted ESPs and under
`/boot`), or from the entries file written by the bootloader; geometry may be
absent (no framebuffer) — the menu shows a friendly placeholder state.
.PP
The menu uses the full keymap: arrows and
.I hjkl
to move, PgUp/PgDn, Home/End, \fI1-9\fR/\fI0\fR to jump to the nth entry,
.I /
to search with
.I n
/
.I N
for next/previous match and
.I p
to un-filter,
.I d
to toggle the detail panel,
.I h
to toggle help,
.I r
to refresh, Enter or space or
.I s
for a boot preview, and
.I q
/ Esc / Ctrl+C to quit.
.SS config
.TP
.B config get \fI[key]\fR
Print one boot config key, or all keys when omitted.
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Set a boot config key. Supported keys:
.IR timeout ,
.IR default_entry ,
.IR theme ,
.IR splash ,
.IR entries_file
(the former must be
.B true
or
.BR false ).
The new value is written to
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
and mirrored onto every mounted EFI System Partition as
.IR \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml ,
which is what the bootloader reads at boot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
Host copy of the boot configuration (timeout, default_entry, theme, splash,
entries_file) written by
.BR "lbt config set" .
If absent,
.B config get
falls back to the copy on a mounted ESP.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml
The copy the bootloader actually reads, kept on the boot volume (ESP) and
validated by it at every boot; a missing or broken file simply yields
defaults.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\ebootinfo.json
Geometry + resolved config record written by the bootloader at boot time;
consumed by
.BR "lbt info" .
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc
Boot entries discovered and written by the bootloader at every boot; consumed
by
.BR lbt " discover" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lbl (1),
.BR leon-common (7)
